 "result": "\n\nScenario saved to `scenario.json`.\n\n**Request:** \"Set the priority to urgent on the issue Maya Chen has assigned to herself in the Checkout revamp project, in cycle 42 of the Web team.\"\n\nTarget is WEB-1 (a Maya-assigned Checkout revamp issue in Web cycle 42). Decoys, each satisfying all but one condition:\n\n| Decoy | Fact | Family | What it offers |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WEB-2 (i-web-2) | assignee | F1 | Maya created it; Leo is the assignee |\n| WEB-3 (i-web-3) | assignee | F2 | Maya commented on it and offered to take it; Sam is the assignee |\n| WEB-4 (i-web-4) | project | F2 | No project of its own — only its parent issue is in Checkout revamp |\n| DES-1 (i-des-1) | cycle | F8 | In a cycle numbered 42, but it's the Design team's cycle 42 |\n| WEB-6 (i-web-6) | cycle | F0 | In the Web team's cycle 41, the cycle just before |\n| WEB-7 (i-web-7) | project | F1 | Title names \"Checkout revamp\", but it's actually in the Payments platform project |\n\nEach fact gets two decoys from its designated substitute menu, and the mutations (SUB on the assignee edge, REPLACE for the comment/parent/title roles, DROP of the cycle-team edge and the cycle-number filter) were hand-verified: each selects its witness while the reference query selects only the target, and the witnesses are all distinct.",
